{"success": true, "name": "arc-panel-mask-validation", "file": "references/aligned-panel-overlap.md", "content": "# Aligned two-panel overlap masks

In separator-split grids with two same-sized panels and output the size of one panel, do not assume the output copies one side. Test foreground-mask relations at each aligned coordinate: intersection, union, and directional differences. The decisive cells are those where exactly one panel is foreground. If output foreground appears only where both panels are foreground across every demo, the rule is an intersection mask; map its output palette separately. Mechanically replay every cell and every demo before applying to the test.

In task-06d696f4, three demos used differing dimensions and colors. In each, output was the cellwise intersection of the top and bottom panel foreground masks, with output foreground recolored to 2 and background to 0. Single-panel-only markers were suppressed. The test prediction should therefore be 2 exactly where the upper panel has 1 and the lower panel has 9; elsewhere 0.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/HA-hermes-luna6-low-rnd0/frozen/held-out/play/users/u022/system/state/hermes/skills/arc/arc-panel-mask-validation/references/aligned-panel-overlap.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "arc-panel-relations", "file": "references/task-a290adda-current-review.md", "content": "# task-a290adda current review: unresolved rule and malformed outputs

In this instance, input was 25x18 with a full separator row (color 1) at row index 12. Above it were 12 rows of background 2 with a lone 9; below it were 12 rows of background 0 with sparse 9s. Two demos had different layouts: a 13x25 grid with an interior full separator row and 13x11 output, and a 13x23 grid with a full separator column and 13x11 output. The demos therefore do not validate a straightforward aligned equality mask for the current test.

Three submissions were rejected: first a purported comparison mask with rows of mixed width (malformed grid), then a too-short all-background output (also malformed), then a 12x18 marker-only guess (rejected). Do not infer an output rule from these guesses. For future recurrence, first derive output dimensions from complete demos, explicitly model separator orientation/position, panel shapes and any cropping, then request a discriminating demo if rule hypotheses remain. Before every submission, mechanically verify dimensions and that all output rows have identical widths. The older skill narrative that marked this task solved conflicts with this current evidence and must not be treated as authoritative.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/HA-hermes-luna6-low-rnd0/frozen/held-out/play/users/u022/system/state/hermes/skills/arc/arc-panel-relations/references/task-a290adda-current-review.md"}
